### 3. Additional context:                                                                                              
The review focuses on diagnostic accuracy of menopausal status, ultrasound, and biomarker tests (alone or in            
combination) for ovarian cancer in symptomatic women with pelvic mass. The screening process emphasized studies that    
directly evaluated test performance (sensitivity, specificity, AUC, etc.) in the target population with appropriate     
reference standards. Excluded studies were primarily methodological papers, reviews, or studies focused on other        
cancers/diagnostic pathways. The decisions were made conservatively: when abstract lacked explicit reference standard or
population details but strongly implied diagnostic accuracy evaluation in relevant population (e.g., studies 82, 85), I 
opted for INCLUDE. All rationales are study-specific and tied to the review's criteria. The tool `batch_screen_studies` 
was used to format the mini-batch prior to decision-making, ensuring structured presentation of studies and selection   
criteria for consistent application.                                                                                    
                                                                                                                        
